main#main
  header.page-hero.page-hero-wide.shell
    span.eyebrow AI agents and product engineering
    h1 I build the workflow around AI.
    p I build skills and repository harnesses for AI coding agents, alongside AI product features. Clear context, permissions, structured outputs, tests, and verification make the work dependable.
  = partial "partials/agent_tools"
  section.section.shell aria-labelledby="ai-toolkit"
    div.section-heading
      div
        span.eyebrow My working toolkit
        h2#ai-toolkit Every tool has a job.
      p I use AI for research, implementation, debugging, and review. I choose the tool for the task, give it relevant context, and verify the result against sources and working software.
    div.skill-groups
      article.skill-group
        h3 Coding and review
        p Codex, Claude Code, and Cursor help me explore codebases, implement focused changes, debug failures, write tests, and review work. Clear scope, repository instructions, and local checks keep the changes reviewable.
      article.skill-group
        h3 Research and learning
        p I use ChatGPT and Claude to explore unfamiliar topics, compare approaches, and turn research into readable notes. Asking different models the same question helps me examine their assumptions and check the evidence behind an answer.
      article.skill-group
        h3 Code and application context
        p
          a href="https://xerj.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" XERJ
          '  helps me retrieve relevant source and reference implementations from indexed repositories.
          a href="https://tidewave.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" Tidewave
          |  adds context from a running Rails or Phoenix app; MCP connects agents to tools and data through explicit access.
      article.skill-group
        h3 Focused execution
        p
          a href="https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" RTK
          '  trims noisy command output before it reaches the agent’s context.
          a href="https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" Ponytail
          |  guides agents toward the smallest complete change, reuse of existing code, and the checks needed to verify the result.
      article.skill-group
        h3 Reusable instructions
        p Skills, AGENTS.md, my Rails Update skill, and my Elixir/Phoenix harness turn recurring work into repeatable workflows. I keep product facts, constraints, and verification steps close to the code.
        a.text-link href="#ai-skills" Browse the skills
      article.skill-group
        h3 Product integrations
        p I use OpenAI and DeepL APIs in localization workflows and build MCP access for product capabilities and SQL databases. Permissions and human review stay part of the surrounding product.
